course: dictionary
lesson: 3855
title: Fourteen: ten plus four
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fourteen is a number. It is ten plus four, and it is one more than thirteen. You can also think of it as two groups of seven, so 14 = 2 × 7.
explain: Fourteen is an even number, so it can be shared into two equal groups. It is not a prime number, because its factors are 1, 2, 7 and 14.
explain: Two weeks have fourteen days, and two weeks is also called a fortnight. Fourteen is a teen number, so it comes after thirteen and before fifteen.
explain: Counting legs helps us sort animals. «A woodlouse with fourteen legs is not an insect either» because a spider has eight legs and an insect has six.
fact: Fourteen means ten plus four, and it is written as 14.
fact: Fourteen is even, and its factors are 1, 2, 7 and 14.
fact: The ordinal form is fourteenth, written as 14th.
fact: «1400» is read as «fourteen hundred», which is 2 pm on a 24-hour clock.
fact: Woodlice are not insects; they are crustaceans, relatives of crabs, and they have fourteen legs.
exercise: Ten plus four makes what? | *14 | 12 | 16 | 104
exercise: How many days are in a fortnight? | 21 | 28 | *14 | 7
exercise: Is fourteen an even number? | *Yes, it can be shared into two equal groups | Yes, but it has only one factor | No, it is odd | No, it is prime
test: Fourteen equals 2 × what? | 6 | *7 | 12 | 8
test: The 24-hour time «1400» is which time? | 12 pm | 1 pm | *2 pm | 4 pm
exam: Which animal with fourteen legs is not an insect? | A spider | A beetle | An ant | *A woodlouse
